  greetings:
  - Eh? Speak up. Detective, is it?
  - Sit down before you fall down.
  aboutSelf: Forty years I was the only doctor for thirty miles. Delivered half this town and sewed up the other half. Every scar in Semblance, I wrote down. Set bones in every root cellar from here to the county line; every farmhouse out here has one.
  aboutTown: People ask why so many of us look the way we do. Inbreeding, they think. It's not. It's the land. The land here keeps what it touches, and changes it a little.
  seenAnythingStrange: Somebody's been in my old surgery files. Put them back in the wrong order. Nobody in this family puts anything back right except me.
  foundersDay: Rained, I'm fairly sure. Or was that '82? They all run together at my age. Mae's cherry pie won, that I'd swear to. I slept through the sermon.
  gossip:
  - title: About Mae Whitlock
    response: Mae wears Earl's ring on her left hand still. I took it off his finger myself, after. She asked for it back the same day.
  - title: About Lyle Pruitt
    response: My grandson's left eye wanders. Born that way. I told his father not to fuss; it'll make him interesting.
